## Task A: I1-Only Analysis — NEW SIGNIFICANT FINDING

### A3: Q4 Maintenance vs Drift — **p = 0.0014** 🔥

| Target Quad | n_drift | n_maint | t-test p | Mann-Whitney p |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Q1 | 90 | 23 | 0.089 | 0.085 |
| **Q4** | **50** | **52** | **0.002** | **0.001** |
| Q3 | 13 | 2 | 0.642 | n/a |

**Q4 (Calm/Relaxed) is the strongest maintenance result.** When viewers transition INTO Q4 from a different quadrant (drift), their valence shift is significantly different from viewers who maintain Q4→Q4.

### A2: Per-Transition Drift Table (top effects)

| Transition | n | Mean Δ I1 Valence | Mean Δ I1 Arousal |
|---|---|---|---|
| Q2→Q1 | 43 | **+1.05** | +0.86 |
| Q3→Q4 | 97 | +0.87 | +0.68 |
| Q3→Q1 | 45 | +0.80 | +1.07 |
| Q2→Q4 | 78 | +0.82 | +0.07 |
| Q4→Q2 | 75 | -0.85 | -0.15 |
| Q1→Q2 | 52 | -0.80 | -0.42 |

### A4: B2 Dominance
B2 rate is ~60-62% regardless of starting bucket or switching status. t-test: p=0.558 (not significant). **B2 projection is a universal constant in sequential clip viewing.**

### A5: Hyp-1 Retest
Mann-Whitney confirms non-significance at τ=0.50 (p=0.483). Approaches significance at τ=0.75 (p=0.055).

